# nr-relay-push-ice-frames: what the wiring applies (nothing here was compiled: cargo was not run)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml (scaffold file, not edited here)

tests/push_ice_frames.rs calls items that exist only with the `test-support` feature (`NativePushService::association_count`).
Add beside the `native_push` entry:

    [[test]]
    name = "push_ice_frames"
    path = "tests/push_ice_frames.rs"
    required-features = ["test-support"]

No other Cargo edit: the module uses mixdog-rt, serde_json and the store already in the crate.

## What the task that assembles the relay (nr-relay-server) calls, once per process, on `hub.dispatch()`

- `mixdog_relay::native_push::frames::register(hub.dispatch(), &service)` with the one `Arc<NativePushService>` (built from
  `NativePush::from_environment`, `None` sender when `is_configured()` is false). It registers the capability (platforms of the
  service; `nativePush` and `nativePushPlatforms` are published only when it is not empty), the frame types `native-push-bind`,
  `native-push-unbind` and `native-push`, and a revoke hook that drops the bindings of a revoked device or client. Returns
  `Err(Rejected)` if a type is taken. A send runs beside the leg's reader and its `native-push-result` goes to the device's live leg.
- `mixdog_relay::ice::frames::register(hub.dispatch(), config)` ONLY when `turn_config_from_env` gave `Ok(Some(config))`
  (on `Err` log `logline::turn_issuance_disabled` and do not register). It registers the `ice` capability and `ice-servers-request`.
  Without the call the relay advertises no ice and ignores the request, as without TURN settings.
- `impl PairedClients for DeviceStore` now lives in native_push/frames.rs (has_client over the store).

## compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING

No protocol method is involved (these are relay wire frames, not app-server methods): no name leaves SERVICE_PENDING.
